{"reference":"Genesis 4","book":"Genesis","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Cain as a negative sibling example","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Cain is received in Scripture as a negative sibling example: his deeds are described as evil while his brother's are described as righteous. That reception makes Cain a warning about hatred within a family, but it must not be turned into antisemitism or inherited blame assigned to later groups.","verse_refs":["Genesis 4:1-16"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_004_90ccff1b9b40a6431459d181"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
